From 856afefd12ce439e12c16dbf9076285858724c1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:18:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(wardens): a clustered task the Queen cancels or fails
 leaves the clustered set

A task Clustering or isolation paused stayed in the Warden's clustered set until a TaskResume
that production never sends, so a Warden whose paused task the Queen then withdrew or failed
(FAIL_TASK sends a TaskCancel) reported CLUSTERED for good. A Queen-sent TaskCancel or
Intervene(CANCEL) now ends the pause too. Appendix C gives CLUSTERED one way out, to ACTIVE,
so a clustered Warden left with nothing settles CLUSTERED -> ACTIVE -> WATCH, each move its own
event, rather than asking for an edge the machine does not have.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EKZW22X7GB1ADCG4ApBsA8
