From 7459f3085461f16a82a7cca8af923b7191bf5682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(wardens): Rebind and Takeover through
 Warden.intervene start the bee they promise

Warden.intervene relayed a Rebind or a Takeover to the bee, which wrote its Handoff and
stopped, and nothing followed it: the task sat RUNNING with no bee, as the Handoff lever did
before round 3. The successor mark is now a SuccessorOrder naming the fresh bee's binding and
whether it is a new attempt: a Handoff carries the same attempt on the same binding, a Rebind
binds the lever's slot and a Takeover the supervisor's own (the Warden's; ADR-0021: a Warden
takes over through a fresh sub-bee), both at attempt+1, with llm.rebound recorded when the
binding changes. The Guard's slot_binding point decides the binding when the fresh bee spawns;
a Drone's set holds llm:worker only, so a Takeover is refused there and reported FAILED with
the Guard's reason and the Handoff, never orphaned. The context check no longer overwrites an
order a lever already gave.

