From 36a1bdce50f74b55abcc3770641962836491ff0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:38:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(queen,wardens): attempt numbers never go backwards on
 the trail

A Warden's own respawn, rebind or Rebind/Takeover recovery numbers its
fresh bee past the Queen's last dispatch, but never told her, so her
next retry numbered from her own count and reused an attempt number the
trail had already seen. The Warden now reports each new attempt on a
TaskProgress(STARTED), as TaskAssign.attempt's own rule asks, and
worker.spawned names the attempt.

The Queen keeps an AttemptBook: her own dispatches of each task (her
ceiling and her policy's rungs count these, so a Warden's respawns never
skip one of her rungs) and the highest attempt number any report or
placement carried, which every retry numbers past. The autopilot table
reads both as an AttemptTally; a FAILED result numbered below the latest
attempt is stale however few dispatches the Queen made.

