From d553dc35367a95e426ddb3d4390c5df0e05b0581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:52:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(workers,wardens): a Drone reports its context every
 model round

A Drone recorded its tokens once, after its tool loop had ended, so no
crossing could ever end the attempt that made it: neither its own
threshold check between tool calls nor its Warden's context check, which
reads each Heartbeat, saw the context mid-loop. Every round now records
its own usage through the call gate the loop already calls: the context
is the latest round's (its input is the whole conversation so far), the
spend the sum of every round's.

The tracked context is cleared when an episode hands off and when a
fresh one starts, so no Heartbeat reports a finished episode's window as
a running bee's; and the Warden orders a compact once per crossing,
since each Heartbeat of a long tool call would otherwise repeat it and
one read late would reset the fresh episode too.

An e2e runs a real Drone on the Hive Stand whose first round fills its
window with no lever pulled: past the threshold it resets itself, short
of it its Warden orders the compact; the resumed episode finishes.

