From fc0239fedd0d3c355792dc19bdd5b7c465e6ab02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:04:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(queen): the Queen holds a Warden's liveness while she
 freezes its Cell

A relayed snapshot or rollback freezes the whole Cell, its Warden too,
for as long as the backend works: 27 s a GiB on the development host,
bounded by nothing the Warden can declare beforehand. It announced its
relay's own wait as its interval, so a longer freeze drew a false
CELL_UNREACHABLE about a silence the Hive itself had caused.

The Queen is the one freezing it, so the Cell listener now wraps its
call into the backend in a liveness hold for that Warden (attach's
frozen_cell, over ticks.liveness.frozen_by_the_hive): never judged while
it lasts, a whole window afresh from the thaw. The Warden's announcement
stays for the moments before the listener reads the request.

Named cell_gate change: listener._dispatch answers both relay kinds
through one branch inside the hold.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EKZW22X7GB1ADCG4ApBsA8
